PRODUCT TYPE NOTES
------------------
- SAREE: keep the drape, pallu, border width, motif scale and blouse piece exactly as
  uploaded. Do not invent a new pattern. Show the saree flat with a soft natural fall.
- PANJABI / KURTA / SHIRT: keep the placket, collar, buttons, cuffs and embroidery
  placement. Show the full length without cropping the hem.
- SHOES / SANDALS: keep the sole, stitching, hardware and shape. Use a three-quarter
  angle and a soft shadow. Do not add laces or buckles that are not there.
- BAGS: keep the handles, straps, hardware and stitching. Show the front and one
  three-quarter view if the prompt allows two images.
- JEWELLERY: keep the metal tone, stone placement and chain length. Do not add stones.
  Use a close-up detail prompt and a clean ivory surface.
- KIDS: keep the same proportions and print placement. Do not shrink or stylise the
  product into a cartoon.

CONSISTENCY RULES
-----------------
- Same camera angle for every colour of the same product.
- Same background tone and light direction for the whole collection.
- Keep the product centred with equal breathing room.
- Use one accent colour per image; never all brand colours at once.
- Preserve the original product's character and fabric.
- If the product has embroidery or a print, keep the pattern exactly as uploaded.
- Generate at 4:5. Do not crop the garment.
- Check the neckline, sleeves and hem after generation. Regenerate if they changed.
- Do not let the model add pockets, belts, buttons, labels or embroidery that were not
  in the original product.
- Do not use pure white backgrounds. The Bengalot look is warm ivory.
- Do not add text, logos, badges, price tags or watermarks.

